// Pull request author: PpT2211
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Local Credential Testing Via Dscl Authonly
// Sigma ID: 7f3a1c2e-9b4d-4e2a-8c6f-1d5e7a9b3c4f
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Pavan Pothamsetti (PpT2211)
// Date: 2026-08-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1110.001
// Description: Detects execution of the macOS "dscl" (Directory Service command line) utility with the
//   "-authonly" flag, which validates local user credentials without creating a full authenticated
//   session. Repeated or unexpected use of this flag can indicate credential validation/brute-force
//   attempts against local accounts, outside of normal administrative activity.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative credential checks or password-reset tooling using dscl
//   - Automated MDM/config-management scripts validating local account credentials
//   - IT helpdesk scripts run as root during account troubleshooting
// References:
//   - https://ss64.com/mac/dscl.html
//   - https://www.jamf.com/blog/crashstealer-macos-infostealer-analysis/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/d327be3a30486bd848551da7abd3bed4bdecec02/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_dscl_authonly.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/dscl" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-authonly") and (not(AccountName =~ "root"))
